Ladybird masks transformed text by grapheme, retaining a mapping to the
DOM source. Blink’s LayoutText::TransformAndSecureText() applies casing
before SecureText(). WebKit selects its masking glyph in RenderText and
applies it in secureText(). Gecko’s nsTextFrame obtains the glyph from
TextSecurityMaskChar() for the text run.

Chrome 157.0.8103.79 and WebKit 26.5 rendered two marks for an
uppercased German sharp s. Firefox 151.0 rendered one. The three
browsers used distinct disc, circle and square marks.

Ladybird paints SVG mask glyphs and exposes their geometry at the
original DOM code-unit indices. With a combining sequence or a
supplementary character followed by x, Firefox 151.0 and WebKit 26.5
exposed all three UTF-16 code units. Chrome 158.0.8127.36 exposed two,
the number of rendered marks.

Gecko counts addressable characters in SVGTextFrame::GetNumberOfChars().
WebKit counts fragment lengths in
SVGTextQuery::numberOfCharactersCallback(). Blink counts inline text in
SvgTextQuery::NumberOfCharacters(). SVG 2 assigns DOM indices before
text transformation.

Ladybird paints one mask for each CRLF pair in text a script creates.
A lone CR and a lone LF each get a mark. Chrome 158.0.8127.36 also
paints one mark for CRLF in LayoutText::SecureText(). Firefox 151.0
and WebKit 26.5 paint two. Gecko masks each character in
nsCaseTransformTextRunFactory::TransformString(). WebKit masks the
characters of the rendered string in RenderText::secureText().

When pre-line preserves a line feed in unmasked text, Ladybird keeps
the line break even when CR and LF form one grapheme. Two CRLF pairs
produce three lines in all three engines, with ASCII or Latin text.
